# Comprehensive 8-bit byte-parity sweep — port vs the real C encoder
Date:    2026-08-03
Host:    darwin arm64 (Apple); C oracle = in-tree SVT-AV1 v4.2.0, Bin/Release
Tool:    tools/identity_full_8bit.sh (default tiers: synthetic + dims)
Files:   identity_full_8bit_2026-08-03.tsv        default gate run (this file)
         identity_full_8bit_dims_2026-08-03.tsv   dims tier WITH p0/p4 added

## Default gate run: 738/738 byte-identical, +2 pinned, 0 harness errors (exit 0)

  synthetic  4 content {uniform,gradient,diag,screen} x {64,128}px
             x qp {5,20,32,48,63} x EVERY preset 0..13   = 560 cells
  dims       15 geometries (32x32 .. 512x512, incl. odd 65x65, straddle
             80x88, both-partial 120x104) x 2 content x qp {20,48}
             x preset {6,9,13}                            = 180 cells

Every preset 0..13 is byte-identical on 64-aligned content at every swept qp,
including q5 and q63. C clamps all-intra presets above M9 to M9
(enc_handle.c:4415-4419) but the PORT does not, so 10..13 were swept as
distinct configurations rather than assumed equal to M9.

## The M9 clamp, MEASURED rather than read

For all 40 (content, size, qp) combinations in the synthetic tier, C's presets
9, 10, 11, 12 and 13 produce byte-IDENTICAL streams — an independent
confirmation of the all-intra clamp at enc_handle.c:4415-4419, from the oracle's
own output rather than from reading its source. Since the port is
byte-identical to C at every one of those presets, the port's p10..p13 output
equals C's M9 output too, even though the port does not implement the clamp.
That is why sweeping 10..13 is worth the cells: it verifies the equivalence
instead of assuming it.

## The 2 pinned cells (self-promoting)

  screen 64x64   q63 p1   C=64B  port=71B
  screen 128x128 q63 p1   C=185B port=193B

The smallest known reproducer of the #71 palette-decision class. Isolated:
p0 and p2 at the same qp are IDENTICAL, and q48/q55 are identical at EVERY
preset. Probe with palette forced off: C=64B port=60B — the port goes SMALLER
than C, so C codes palette here too and the two simply decide differently.

## dims tier WITH the unclaimed band (IF_PRESETS="0 4"): 244/300

  p6/p9/p13  60/60 each — every geometry, every qp
  p0 30/60, p4 34/60, splitting into two already-known classes:
    53  partial-SB at p0/p4 — presets 0-5 skip the C-faithful PD1 walk on a
        non-64-aligned SB (pipeline.rs `refined` requires full_sb), so the
        search is structurally different. docs/arbitrary-dims-port-map.md.
    3   ALIGNED, all `screen` at 256/384/512 — the #71 screen-content RD
        class, same as the production corpus sees on its M0 screen classes.
  No unexplained class.

## Two panics this sweep found and fixed (crates/svtav1-encoder/src/intrabc_hash.rs)

C computes `x_end = pic_width - block_size + 1` as a SIGNED int
(hash_motion.c:195-196, :222-223); negative means the loop body never runs. The
port used `usize`, so it underflowed and wrapped to ~2^64. On a 32x32 screen
frame at preset 0, through the PUBLIC encode API:
  generate_block_hash_value              index out of bounds: len 1024, index 1024
  add_to_hash_map_by_row_with_precal     index out of bounds: len 1024, index 2048
No earlier gate encoded anything below 60x60 with the screen-content tools armed.

## REAL-CORPUS TIER (IF_TIER=real, IF_REAL_N=6): 403/450, 0 harness errors
File: identity_full_8bit_real_2026-08-03.tsv
18 images x 512x512 centre crop x qp {5,20,32,48,63} x preset {0,4,6,10,13}

                p0      p4      p6      p10     p13
  gb82-photo    30/30   30/30   30/30   30/30   30/30
  CID22-photo   26/30   26/30   30/30   30/30   30/30
  gb82-screen   10/30   11/30   30/30   30/30   30/30

**At preset 6 and above the port is byte-identical to C on EVERY real image
tested — photographic and screen, at every qp from 5 to 63.** The entire gap is
presets 0 and 4, and it is the two already-known classes:

  - gb82-screen p0/p4 (39 cells) — the #71 palette/IBC calibration class, the
    same one tools/screen_ibc_gate.sh pins. codec_wiki and gmessages are 25/25
    (they are the non-sc_class5 controls); graph, gui, imac_dark and imac_g3
    diverge by roughly +-1%.
  - CID22 1028637.png (8 cells) — a photo RD near-tie band, +-0.4%, at p0/p4
    only. The other five CID22 images and all six gb82 photos are 25/25.

Magnitudes are small and BOTH directions (the port is smaller than C about as
often as larger), which is the signature of a near-tie rather than a systematic
mis-cost.
